<title>JAPAN: Output at big Japan aluminium mills surges in July.</title>
<headline>Output at big Japan aluminium mills surges in July.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Output of fabricated aluminium products at Japan's seven leading mills surged 10.1 percent in July from the same month last year to a record 146,946 tonnes, according to data submitted by the companies to the Japan Aluminum Federation and released on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It was the 13th consecutive monthly rise. The previous record was set in June 1997.</p>
<p>The July data was as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     July 97	 yr/yr change</p>
<p> Total	    146,946	 +10.1 pct</p>
<p> Flat-rolled    117,417	 +10.6 pct</p>
<p>   Can stock     40,528	  -2.0 pct</p>
<p> Extrusions	29,529	  +8.4 pct</p>
<p>The seven companies are: Kobe Steel Ltd (includes KAAL, a joint venture with Aluminum Co of America ), Sumitomo Light Metal Industries Ltd, Furukawa Electric Co, Mitsubishi Aluminum Co, Nippon Light Metal Co, Sky Aluminium Co and Showa Aluminum Corp.</p>
